#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0139 expect=noViolation domain=PC
#note "Authority: SEND Conformance Rules v5.0 SEND139 (Condition: POOLID exists in any domain; Rule: POOLID exists in POOLDEF; and a record exists for each subject in POOLID). Partially Executable (underreporting): the Check covers only the first half; here every pool in use has a POOLDEF record for each of its member subjects, so the unchecked half is not violated (plan §2.4). Primary is PC, not POOLDEF: the rule scope is ALL and includes POOLDEF itself, where the foreign and primary readings agree (scope-ALL trap, plan §2.2). Rows 1-2 are pooled records of POOL1 and POOL2, both defined in POOLDEF; row 3 is an individual-subject record with no POOLID."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
dataset PC class=FINDINGS label="Pharmacokinetics Concentrations"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col POOLID   type=Char label="Pool Identifier"
col PCSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col PCTESTCD type=Char label="Test Short Name"
col PCTEST   type=Char label="Test Name"
col PCORRES  type=Char label="Result or Finding in Original Units"
---
S1 | PC |        | POOL1 | 1 | DRUGX | Drug X | 12.5
S1 | PC |        | POOL2 | 2 | DRUGX | Drug X | 13.1
S1 | PC | S1-005 |       | 1 | DRUGX | Drug X | 11.0
---

dataset POOLDEF label="Pool Definition"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col POOLID  type=Char label="Pool Identifier"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
---
S1 | POOL1 | S1-001
S1 | POOL1 | S1-002
S1 | POOL2 | S1-003
S1 | POOL2 | S1-004
---
